note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR GPL-2.0-only
note ident: is this PCI function the GB10 GPU? Decided before any register write, in two stages.
note stage 0 uses PCI facts only (no MMIO). stage 1 adds the two identity registers read from BAR0.
note Result 0 = accept. Otherwise the first failed check:
note 1 vendor is not NVIDIA 0x10de. 2 device is not GB10 0x2e12 (lspci -nn on the Spark 2026-10-21).
note 3 BAR0 is not 64 MiB (the GB10 has only BAR0, 0x24000000-0x27ffffff). 4 stage is not 0 or 1.
note 5 PMC_BOOT_0 reads 0 or all ones (no answer).
note 6 PMC_BOOT_42 ARCHITECTURE 29:24 is not GB200 0x1b (Spark GPUID.TXT: BOOT_0=0x1bb000a1, BOOT_42=0x1bba1000).
note   GB100 0x1a with implementation 0xb is GB10B, another chip: this module's start-up (om/boot.om) and
note   boot package (tools/package.sh) are GB20B's, so it is refused here, before any register write.
note 7 PMC_BOOT_42 IMPLEMENTATION 23:20 is not 0xb (GB20B).
note Sources (open-gpu-kernel-modules 580.173.02, MIT): src/common/inc/swref/published/nv_ref.h:153,170,182;
note src/nvidia/generated/g_hal_archimpl.h:88 (GB10B = ARCHITECTURE_GB100 with IMPLEMENTATION_B) and :96 (GB20B =
note ARCHITECTURE_GB200 with IMPLEMENTATION_B). Read on the Spark's bare metal 2026-11-12T05:45Z: boot0 1bb000a1,
note boot42 1bba1000, i.e. architecture 0x1b, implementation 0xb (docs/evidence/GPUID-20261112T054515Z.TXT).
note Decimal values: 0x10de 4318, 0x2e12 11794, 64 MiB 67108864, 0xffffffff 4294967295, 0x1a 26, 0x1b 27, 0xb 11,
note 0x3f 63 (aien-calc receipts in docs/calc-receipts, listed in docs/STATUS.md).
fn agpu_ident vendor ulong device ulong barlen ulong boot0 ulong boot42 ulong stage ulong to ulong
if ne vendor 4318
ret 1
end
if ne device 11794
ret 2
end
if ne barlen 67108864
ret 3
end
if eq stage 0
ret 0
end
if ne stage 1
ret 4
end
if or eq boot0 0 eq boot0 4294967295
ret 5
end
arch = and shr boot42 24 63
if ne arch 27
ret 6
end
if ne and shr boot42 20 15 11
ret 7
end
ret 0
end
